    "title": "Track A: assert platform default PQBTC data directory names",
    "body": "## Confidence gap\n\n`feature_config_args.py` owns the PQBTC configuration namespace but does not assert the platform-specific default data-directory namespace emitted at startup.\n\n## Owner\n\n@scottdhughes\n\n## Bounded contract\n\n- Assert `.pqbtc` on Linux and other Unix-like platforms.\n- Assert `Library/Application Support/PQBTC` on macOS.\n- Assert `PQBTC` under the Windows roaming legacy path when it exists, otherwise the local application-data path.\n- Retain the two synthetic-environment Windows skips because production resolves those folders through `SHGetSpecialFolderPathW`.\n\n## Non-goals\n\n- No production data-directory behavior change.\n- No inventory policy-class change.\n- No attempt to make Windows shell environment variables override the shell-folder API.\n\n## Validation\n\n- `git diff --check`\n- `python3 ci/test/check_ci_inventory.py`\n- `build/test/functional/test_runner.py --jobs=1 feature_config_args.py`\n- Full branch promotion matrix, including Windows and macOS.\n\n## Acceptance\n\nThe targeted test and complete branch matrix pass, and posture/status documentation records the narrowed residual boundary.",
